{"module":"world","voice":"male","duration":235.1,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"A world system","start":0.0,"end":1.17,"words":[[0.04,0.21],[0.21,0.56],[0.56,1.08]]},{"el":"intro","text":"American racism was part of a global system of empire.","start":1.97,"end":6.13,"words":[[2.02,2.62],[2.62,3.21],[3.21,3.43],[3.43,3.65],[3.65,3.8],[3.8,3.95],[3.95,4.47],[4.47,4.92],[4.92,5.06],[5.06,5.58]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Seeing that system helps explain why the same patterns appear on every continent, and what other countries have tried in order to repair them.","start":6.48,"end":14.64,"words":[[6.52,6.88],[6.88,7.1],[7.1,7.53],[7.53,7.89],[7.89,8.46],[8.46,8.68],[8.68,8.82],[8.82,9.11],[9.11,9.55],[9.55,9.83],[9.83,9.98],[9.98,10.27],[10.27,10.99],[11.24,11.45],[11.45,11.67],[11.67,11.89],[11.89,12.39],[12.39,12.61],[12.61,12.97],[12.97,13.11],[13.11,13.33],[13.33,13.47],[13.47,13.83],[13.83,14.12]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Abolition paid the enslavers","start":14.99,"end":17.34,"words":[[15.03,15.76],[15.76,16.12],[16.12,16.31],[16.31,17.13]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Britain banned the slave trade in 1807 and slavery in most of its colonies in 1833.","start":18.04,"end":24.48,"words":[[18.1,18.53],[18.53,18.82],[18.82,18.96],[18.96,19.32],[19.32,19.68],[19.68,19.82],[19.82,20.69],[20.69,20.9],[20.9,21.48],[21.48,21.62],[21.62,21.98],[21.98,22.12],[22.12,22.34],[22.34,22.84],[22.84,22.99],[22.99,23.92]]},{"el":"s0","text":"It paid £20 million in compensation, about 40% of the government's annual budget, to slaveholders, not to the people they had enslaved.","start":24.83,"end":35.05,"words":[[24.88,25.02],[25.02,25.32],[25.32,26.12],[26.12,26.55],[26.55,26.7],[26.7,27.65],[27.9,28.26],[28.26,28.99],[28.99,29.14],[29.14,29.28],[29.28,30.01],[30.01,30.45],[30.45,30.96],[31.21,31.36],[31.36,32.3],[32.56,32.78],[32.78,32.92],[32.92,33.07],[33.07,33.43],[33.43,33.65],[33.65,33.87],[33.87,34.52]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The loan raised to pay it was not fully paid off until 2015.","start":35.4,"end":40.05,"words":[[35.45,35.6],[35.6,35.9],[35.9,36.29],[36.29,36.44],[36.44,36.67],[36.67,36.82],[36.82,37.05],[37.05,37.28],[37.28,37.58],[37.58,37.89],[37.89,38.04],[38.04,38.42],[38.42,39.41]]},{"el":"s0","text":"France forced Haiti to pay for its own freedom (see the module “Before race”).","start":40.4,"end":45.74,"words":[[40.43,40.88],[40.88,41.24],[41.24,41.68],[41.68,41.86],[41.86,42.13],[42.13,42.31],[42.31,42.57],[42.57,42.84],[42.84,43.38],[43.38,43.56],[43.56,43.73],[43.73,44.27],[44.27,44.63],[44.63,45.07]]},{"el":"h1","text":"The scramble for Africa","start":46.64,"end":48.28,"words":[[46.69,46.84],[46.84,47.45],[47.45,47.6],[47.6,48.06]]},{"el":"s1","text":"At the Berlin Conference (1884–85), European powers set rules for dividing Africa among themselves, with no Africans present.","start":48.98,"end":60.58,"words":[[49.01,49.2],[49.2,49.38],[49.38,49.85],[49.85,50.59],[50.59,52.64],[52.96,53.8],[53.8,54.27],[54.27,54.55],[54.55,54.92],[54.92,55.1],[55.1,55.85],[55.85,56.41],[56.41,56.78],[56.78,57.62],[57.94,58.22],[58.22,58.5],[58.5,59.24],[59.24,59.99]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In King Leopold II's Congo Free State, forced rubber collection brought mass killing, mutilation and famine; estimates of the dead range widely, from about 1 million to 10 million.","start":60.93,"end":73.77,"words":[[60.98,61.13],[61.13,61.37],[61.37,61.99],[61.99,62.61],[62.61,63.08],[63.08,63.31],[63.31,63.78],[64.05,64.36],[64.36,64.67],[64.67,65.29],[65.29,65.6],[65.6,65.84],[65.84,66.3],[66.57,67.43],[67.43,67.66],[67.66,68.13],[68.4,69.02],[69.02,69.18],[69.18,69.33],[69.33,69.57],[69.57,70.03],[70.03,70.58],[70.85,71.16],[71.16,71.55],[71.55,71.78],[71.78,72.25],[72.25,72.4],[72.4,72.64],[72.64,73.18]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In German South West Africa (Namibia), German troops killed tens of thousands of Herero and Nama people in 1904–08; Germany acknowledged it as genocide in 2021.","start":74.12,"end":86.11,"words":[[74.17,74.31],[74.31,74.74],[74.74,75.03],[75.03,75.32],[75.32,75.75],[75.75,76.33],[76.58,77.01],[77.01,77.37],[77.37,77.66],[77.66,77.95],[77.95,78.09],[78.09,78.67],[78.67,78.82],[78.82,79.25],[79.25,79.46],[79.46,79.75],[79.75,80.11],[80.11,80.26],[80.26,81.91],[82.17,82.67],[82.67,83.32],[83.32,83.46],[83.46,83.61],[83.61,84.25],[84.25,84.4],[84.4,85.55]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Hitler's American model","start":87.01,"end":88.71,"words":[[87.06,87.53],[87.53,88.16],[88.16,88.55]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Law professor James Q.","start":89.41,"end":91.54,"words":[[89.47,89.62],[89.62,90.17],[90.17,90.63],[90.63,90.94]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Whitman showed in 2017 that Nazi lawyers drafting the 1935 Nuremberg Laws studied American race law, including state bans on interracial marriage, Jim Crow, and race-based immigration and citizenship rules.","start":91.89,"end":107.81,"words":[[91.94,92.42],[92.42,92.73],[92.73,92.89],[92.89,94.0],[94.0,94.24],[94.24,94.64],[94.64,95.03],[95.03,95.59],[95.59,95.75],[95.75,96.93],[96.93,97.73],[97.73,97.96],[97.96,98.44],[98.44,99.07],[99.07,99.39],[99.39,99.63],[99.9,100.54],[100.54,100.93],[100.93,101.25],[101.25,101.41],[101.41,102.2],[102.2,102.76],[103.03,103.35],[103.35,103.75],[104.02,104.26],[104.26,104.97],[104.97,105.77],[105.77,106.0],[106.0,106.8],[106.8,107.19]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Some of them found U.S. law harsher than they were prepared to go, for example in its “one drop” definitions of race.","start":108.16,"end":116.26,"words":[[108.22,108.46],[108.46,108.63],[108.63,108.87],[108.87,109.28],[109.28,109.69],[110.1,110.26],[110.26,110.59],[110.59,110.83],[110.83,111.07],[111.07,111.24],[111.24,111.81],[111.81,111.97],[111.97,112.3],[112.58,112.75],[112.75,113.4],[113.4,113.56],[113.56,113.81],[113.81,114.05],[114.05,114.38],[114.38,115.19],[115.19,115.36],[115.36,115.76]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Apartheid, and the world's response","start":117.16,"end":120.77,"words":[[117.21,118.16],[118.58,118.93],[118.93,119.17],[119.17,119.77],[119.77,120.6]]},{"el":"s3","text":"South Africa's apartheid system (1948–1994) classified every person by race and confined Black South Africans to “homelands.”","start":121.47,"end":132.79,"words":[[121.52,121.87],[121.87,122.47],[122.47,123.08],[123.08,123.6],[123.6,126.36],[126.66,127.44],[127.44,127.78],[127.78,128.22],[128.22,128.47],[128.47,128.82],[128.82,129.08],[129.08,129.77],[129.77,130.12],[130.12,130.46],[130.46,131.15],[131.15,131.32],[131.32,132.19]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Police killed 69 protesters at Sharpeville in 1960.","start":133.14,"end":137.94,"words":[[133.19,133.6],[133.6,133.92],[133.92,134.72],[134.72,135.44],[135.44,135.6],[135.6,136.09],[136.09,136.25],[136.25,137.37]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A global divestment movement, led in the U.S. by students, churches and the Congressional Black Caucus, pushed Congress to pass sanctions in 1986 over President Reagan's veto.","start":138.29,"end":150.87,"words":[[138.34,138.48],[138.48,138.98],[138.98,139.76],[139.76,140.33],[140.57,140.79],[140.79,140.93],[140.93,141.07],[141.07,141.43],[141.78,141.99],[141.99,142.7],[142.95,143.45],[143.45,143.66],[143.66,143.8],[143.8,144.58],[144.58,144.87],[144.87,145.29],[145.54,145.83],[145.83,146.32],[146.32,146.46],[146.46,146.68],[146.68,147.25],[147.25,147.39],[147.39,148.45],[148.45,148.74],[148.74,149.37],[149.37,149.87],[149.87,150.3]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Nelson Mandela was freed in 1990 and elected president in 1994, and a Truth and Reconciliation Commission followed.","start":151.22,"end":160.84,"words":[[151.27,151.74],[151.74,152.28],[152.28,152.51],[152.51,152.82],[152.82,152.97],[152.97,153.98],[153.98,154.21],[154.21,154.75],[154.75,155.45],[155.45,155.6],[155.6,156.84],[157.11,157.34],[157.34,157.49],[157.49,157.8],[157.8,158.04],[158.04,159.19],[159.19,159.74],[159.74,160.28]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Other settler nations","start":161.74,"end":163.26,"words":[[161.79,162.04],[162.04,162.46],[162.46,163.05]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Australia's “White Australia” policy restricted non-European immigration from 1901 into the 1970s, and its governments removed Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander children from their families (the Stolen Generations); Prime Minister Kevin Rudd apologized in 2008.","start":163.96,"end":183.46,"words":[[164.01,164.76],[164.76,165.07],[165.07,165.75],[165.75,166.2],[166.2,166.95],[166.95,167.86],[167.86,168.62],[168.62,168.92],[168.92,169.83],[169.83,170.13],[170.13,170.28],[170.28,171.49],[171.75,171.98],[171.98,172.21],[172.21,172.96],[172.96,173.41],[173.41,174.25],[174.25,174.47],[174.47,174.85],[174.85,175.3],[175.3,175.83],[175.83,176.44],[176.44,176.74],[176.74,176.97],[176.97,177.49],[177.49,177.65],[177.65,178.17],[178.17,179.16],[179.42,179.8],[179.8,180.33],[180.33,180.71],[180.71,180.93],[180.93,181.76],[181.76,181.91],[181.91,182.9]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In Canada about 150,000 Indigenous children were sent to residential schools; the Truth and Reconciliation Commission called it cultural genocide in 2015, and Pope Francis apologized in 2022.","start":183.81,"end":197.94,"words":[[183.86,184.0],[184.0,184.41],[184.41,184.75],[184.75,186.4],[186.4,187.09],[187.09,187.63],[187.63,187.77],[187.77,188.05],[188.05,188.18],[188.18,188.87],[188.87,189.28],[189.52,189.66],[189.66,189.93],[189.93,190.14],[190.14,191.17],[191.17,191.65],[191.65,191.92],[191.92,192.06],[192.06,192.67],[192.67,193.29],[193.29,193.43],[193.43,194.32],[194.56,194.76],[194.76,195.04],[195.04,195.52],[195.52,196.27],[196.27,196.41],[196.41,197.44]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Can repair work?","start":198.84,"end":200.13,"words":[[198.88,199.07],[199.07,199.39],[199.39,199.64]]},{"el":"s5","text":"West Germany began paying reparations to Israel and Holocaust survivors in 1952.","start":200.83,"end":207.24,"words":[[200.88,201.19],[201.19,201.73],[201.73,202.11],[202.11,202.49],[202.49,203.34],[203.34,203.49],[203.49,203.95],[203.95,204.18],[204.18,204.79],[204.79,205.41],[205.41,205.56],[205.56,206.71]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Caribbean nations (CARICOM) adopted a ten-point reparations plan in 2013.","start":207.59,"end":213.35,"words":[[207.64,208.23],[208.23,208.74],[208.74,209.26],[209.51,210.03],[210.03,210.17],[210.17,210.76],[210.76,211.57],[211.57,211.86],[211.86,212.01],[212.01,212.89]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Germany pledged about €1.1 billion in development aid to Namibia in 2021, which many Herero and Nama leaders rejected as inadequate.","start":213.7,"end":223.37,"words":[[213.73,214.2],[214.2,214.6],[214.6,214.94],[214.94,216.15],[216.15,216.55],[216.55,216.69],[216.69,217.43],[217.43,217.63],[217.63,217.76],[217.76,218.23],[218.23,218.37],[218.37,219.44],[219.68,219.95],[219.95,220.22],[220.22,220.62],[220.62,220.82],[220.82,221.09],[221.09,221.43],[221.43,222.03],[222.03,222.17],[222.17,222.84]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Whether reparations, apologies and truth commissions repair harm, and in what form, is actively debated.","start":223.72,"end":231.38,"words":[[223.77,224.08],[224.08,225.02],[225.3,226.0],[226.0,226.24],[226.24,226.55],[226.55,227.18],[227.18,227.57],[227.57,227.88],[228.16,228.39],[228.39,228.55],[228.55,228.78],[228.78,229.1],[229.37,229.53],[229.53,230.08],[230.08,230.78]]},{"el":"s5","text":"The precedents themselves are documented.","start":231.73,"end":234.24,"words":[[231.78,231.9],[231.9,232.5],[232.5,232.98],[232.98,233.04],[233.04,233.76]]}]}